Continue task 1 with the native mocked-provider suite plus two production corrections.

Production corrections:
1. Convert the Upstash atomic transact member to the Effect-language-service recommended Effect.fn("AtomicKeyValueStore.transact")(generator, pipeTransformation) form, then pass the named function to AtomicKeyValueStore.of. Keep safe mapError and span in the Effect.fn transformation.
2. In scanKeys, after decoding a page, reject the page as a provider failure if any returned key does not start with options.keyPrefix. Use Effect Array.every. This is required for namespace isolation even if Redis MATCH is violated.
3. Add standard repository metadata to package.json matching sibling packages.

Add test/upstash-key-value-store.test.ts using makeUpstashPersistenceLayer and a narrow mock:
- exact prefixed get/set/remove operations and native get null->undefined;
- one clientFactory call per Layer build;
- complete multi-page cursor scan, duplicate-page key de-dup, size result, exact prefix match/count;
- clear collects all pages before DEL, de-dupes keys, chunks >100 keys, and empty namespace makes no DEL;
- malformed get, malformed scan page, out-of-prefix scan result, and rejected provider Promise map to safe KeyValueStoreError with method/message only and no key/cause/private marker in Schema.UnknownFromJsonString rendering;
- prefix Schema accepts a normal prefix and rejects *, ?, [, ], and backslash;
- no FLUSHDB/DBSIZE/unscoped command can be represented by the narrow client/calls.

Use Effect/test patterns, Schema codecs, no JSON.parse/stringify, unsafe casts, suppressions, raw DTO mirror, or production test export. Test helpers may simulate provider state but keep them test-owned and concise.

